    "description": "Estimated camera spectral sensitivity, NOT a measurement. Fitted so that the IDT matrices these curves would receive (Academy P-2013-001-style CIE Lab fit, rawtoaces 190-patch training set) reproduce ARRI's 2013 ALEXA native->ACES AP0 matrices at 17 CCTs, under a 4-component PCA prior built from the 52 Apache-2.0 curves in rawtoaces-data. Each channel normalised to peak 1; relative channel gains are not identifiable from white-balanced matrices and are not needed for white-balanced emulation. The red channel is moved by a hue push (owner decision 2026-10-25): inside the family of curves that agree with ARRI's matrices, the curve that renders orange, red and ochre reflectances 1.5 degrees of CIELAB hue toward yellow, with matrix RMS 0.0092 per coefficient (the 24-variant ensemble spans 0.0064 to 0.0093). See README for accuracy and caveats.",
